4. LongBench does not cover 64K–128K; those cells rely on synthetic benchmarks (RULER/NIAH).
5. Per-step attention mismatch (A1 attends to k_r·u << K) only partially resolved via compute-matched sensitivity analysis.
6. FP16 KV assumed; quantization changes the budget.
7. RULER/NIAH are synthetic; LongBench provides external validity but with shorter documents.

## 8. Assumptions (separate from fixed requirements)
- Compute: 4×A100/H100 80GB, ~2 weeks; fallback 1 GPU.
- Model: LLaMA-3 8B primary; 70B optional.
- InfLLM: v2 as primary system (B4); v1 units as a level (B1–B3 approximations).
